```

The new channel test group (`chatgpt_oauth_flow_test.dart`, "the fah/web_auth_session channel" group) covers success, dismiss, bind-failure, channel-error, foreign-state and OAuth-error callbacks — but never "callback lands, then `exchangeFn` throws". The only exchange-failure coverage is the flow-level test where a **fake** `systemSessionFn` invokes `onExchangeError` by hand. That means if the real hop ever stops wiring `onExchangeError` (e.g. a refactor drops the callback), no test fails and the user gets a silently-dead sign-in with no snackbar.

