{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: assert on the shared constant instead of a string literal**

```dart
expect(
  find.textContaining('Passkey sign-in (Face ID) is not available'),
  findsOneWidget,
);
```

Both new AC2 tests (this file and `codemie_sso_webview_page_test.dart:240`) hard-code a prefix of the copy. Importing `oauthWebViewPasskeyNotice` from `oauth_webview_scaffold.dart` keeps the assertion refactor-safe while the golden still pins the exact pixels:

```dart
expect(find.textContaining(oauthWebViewPasskeyNotice), findsOneWidget);
// or, exact:
expect(find.text(oauthWebViewPasskeyNotice), findsOneWidget);
```

If the literal is deliberate copy-pinning (any copy drift must update the test), fine to keep — but then say so in a comment so the next reader doesn't "fix" it. Same applies to the CodeMie twin. Non-blocking.
